<p>During <code>pnpm dev</code>, saving a <code>.twig</code> file updates the page in place, with no full reload.</p>

<h2>How it works</h2>
<ol>
  <li>Vite notices the changed template and sends a <code>morphdom</code> event to the browser.</li>
  <li>The browser fetches the current URL again and diffs the new <code>&lt;body&gt;</code> into the page with <a href="https://github.com/patrick-steele-idem/morphdom">morphdom</a>.</li>
  <li>The Tailwind stylesheet is reloaded, so new utility classes apply right away.</li>
  <li><code>Drupal.attachBehaviors()</code> runs for the new markup.</li>
</ol>

{% include preview with { demo: 'twig-hmr', title: 'Edit templates/demos/twig-hmr.html.twig' } %}

<h2>Requirements</h2>
<ul>
  <li><code>morphdom</code> installed in your theme.</li>
  <li>A cache clear after starting the dev server, so Drupal loads the assets from Vite.</li>
  <li>Twig cache disabled (<em>Configuration → Development settings</em>), otherwise Drupal returns the old markup.</li>
  <li>Your behaviors must be idempotent. Use <code>once()</code>, because they run again after every update.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Running the dev server in DDEV</h2>
<p>Start Vite inside the web container, so <code>DDEV_PRIMARY_URL</code> is set and the assets are served over HTTPS on the port exposed in <code>.ddev/config.vite.yml</code>. Then clear the cache:</p>
{% embed code_block with { lang: 'sh' } %}{% block code %}{% verbatim %}
ddev exec -d /var/www/html/drupal/web/themes/custom/uebertool_docs \
  "./node_modules/.bin/uebertool && ./node_modules/.bin/vite"
ddev drush cr
{% endverbatim %}{% endblock %}{% endembed %}

<p>Turn it off with:</p>
{% embed code_block with { lang: 'ts', title: 'vite.config.ts' } %}{% block code %}{% verbatim %}
uebertool({
  features: {
    twighmr: false,
  },
})
{% endverbatim %}{% endblock %}{% endembed %}

{% embed aside %}
  {% block content %}
    <p>Pages whose URL contains <code>/iframe.html</code> (Storybook) are skipped.</p>
  {% endblock %}
{% endembed %}
